## Purpose

Final repository hygiene and judge-facing evidence synchronization before video / Devpost handoff.

The audit found one real release blocker plus stale documentation. No feature work is included.

## Final audited runtime candidate

`e139fa99bd666505ed83a18188423722405695a2`

Policy `0.2.0`.

### Release blocker fixed

`src/toxicjoin/benchmark/evidence.py` still embedded the pre-P0 benchmark identity (`policy_version=0.1.0` and the obsolete report SHA), even though `/api/benchmark/summary` serves that object directly to the fixture judge and the actual release policy/benchmark are `0.2.0`.

The repository consistency test exposed the mismatch during cleanup. The fix changes only the packaged benchmark identity:

- policy `0.1.0` → `0.2.0`;
- report SHA → `3aadc0b357db50641c8ffdc0525dde0e3d9159f933abf62a31a6a74b777d1b08`.

No parser, policy rule, rewriter, executor, verifier, authentication, disclosure, DataHub integration, dependency, Docker, or workflow behavior changed.

## Exact-head validation after fix

All applicable gates passed on `e139fa99bd666505ed83a18188423722405695a2`:

- CI `30140102648` — Python 3.11, Python 3.12, Web, hardened Container;
- CodeQL `30140102673`;
- Supply Chain Security `30140102634`;
- Governance Dependency `30140102647`;
- Adversarial Mutation `30140102676`;
- Compositional Ablation `30140102635`.

Exact-head benchmark artifact:

- ID `8614180997`;
- digest `sha256:3adec180defa9338fe970068f47bc3a479ceae2817941f41b8c7f32c8f4a10d6`;
- 30/30 expected initial decisions/outcomes/reasons;
- zero false allows;
- zero unsafe effective allows;
- report SHA unchanged at `3aadc0b357db50641c8ffdc0525dde0e3d9159f933abf62a31a6a74b777d1b08`.

Exact-head governance/adversarial/ablation artifacts also reproduced the same report hashes as the previous validated baseline.

## Deep-security baseline retained honestly

`fe4f8da2579e09bdbfb1d998b92dfea86549733b`

This otherwise-identical runtime baseline passed the full P4/P5 deep validation:

- Disclosure Sequence `30136824441`;
- Live DataHub `30136824466`;
- Live Agent Registry `30136824472`;
- Hosted Replay `30136824439`;
- frozen external 24-task v2 `30137303763` PASS;
- exact-image black-box pentest `30138071361` — 24/24 PASS.

Those results are not falsely relabeled as reruns on `e139fa99…`. Their applicability is documented explicitly: the later runtime correction only changes the unrestricted fixture benchmark-summary constant; the deep DataHub/security/external-validation paths did not change.

## Documentation/evidence cleanup

- corrected `/api/health` (liveness only) vs `/api/ready` contract;
- corrected judge guide from policy `0.1.0` to `0.2.0`;
- synchronized README and agent-integration contract;
- synchronized locked Live DataHub reproduction guide and schema `1.3` evidence;
- replaced stale benchmark/governance/adversarial/ablation/Live DataHub committed evidence with final measured artifacts;
- added authoritative `docs/evidence/release-candidate.md`;
- synchronized judge evidence matrix and runtime/baseline provenance.

## Repository hygiene outside the diff

- superseded PRs #10, #16, #31 closed without merge;
- Dependabot PRs #56–#66 closed without merge for competition freeze; Dependabot remains enabled;
- roadmap issue #1 updated to final runtime candidate and current release-close tasks.

## Final merge gate

Commits after `e139fa99…` are documentation/evidence-only. Before merge:

- changed-file review must confirm the only runtime-source file is `src/toxicjoin/benchmark/evidence.py`;
- final PR head CI/checks must be green;
- no unresolved review blockers;
- then promote the branch without force.

Devpost remains **NOT SUBMITTED** pending explicit owner review and approval.
